== fusion_inside_and
# (b ##0 c) is the single sample 0; ##1 d ends at 1: the and ends at 1.
property: a |-> (b ##0 c) and (##1 d)
clause: 16.7 16.9.5 16.12.7
class: normative
signals: a b c d
sample : 0 1 2
a      : 1 . .
b      : 1 . .
c      : 1 . .
d      : . 1 .
pass   : . 1 .

== fusion_inside_and_fails
property: a |-> (b ##0 c) and (##1 d)
clause: 16.7 16.9.5 16.12.7
class: normative
signals: a b c d
sample : 0 1 2
a      : 1 . .
b      : 1 . .
c      : . . .
d      : . 1 .
fail   : 1 . .

== intersect_of_goto_2_and_goto_3_never_matches
# req at 0 starts the consequent at 1. ack is high at 1, 2 and 3: ack[->2] can only end at 2
# (the second ack), ack[->3] not before 3 (the third), so the two never end together and
# the intersect has no match; the attempt fails at the second ack, sample 2 (16.12.2).
# The goto repetitions make the consequent unbounded, hence the per-attempt scope.
property: req |=> (ack[->2] intersect ack[->3]) ##0 val
clause: 16.9.6 16.9.2 16.12.2
class: normative
origin: EBMC regression pending_intersect1, hand-derived
signals: req ack val
scope: attempt
sample  : 0 1 2 3 4
req     : 1 . . . .
ack     : . 1 1 1 .
val     : 1 1 1 1 1
outcome : F t t t t
decided : 2 1 2 3 4
fail    : . . 1 . .
pass    : . . . . .
pending: 0
final-fail: 0
